course: dictionary
lesson: 2777
title: Hidden meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A disguise is something that changes how you look, so people do not know who you really are. It can be a costume, a mask or make-up. As a verb, to disguise yourself means to change your look so you are not known.
explain: «Toad of Toad Hall, going about the country disguised as a washerwoman!» Toad changes his appearance so that nobody recognises him. The clue is the word disguised: he is pretending to be someone else.
explain: Disguise can also mean hiding what something really is. «Big French numbers are little sums in disguise.» Quatre-vingt-dix-sept looks hard, but it is really 4 × 20 + 10 + 7 = 97. The sum is hidden inside the word.
fact: A disguise is a noun, meaning clothes, a mask or make-up that make you look like someone else.
fact: To disguise something means to hide what it really is.
fact: «Disguised» means changed in appearance so that you are not known.
fact: «A blessing in disguise» means a bad thing that may turn out to be good.
fact: Some animals disguise themselves with camouflage, so they are hard to spot.
exercise: «The spy wore a disguise to get into the castle.» What is a disguise? | A secret map of the castle | * Clothes, a mask or make-up that change how you look | A tall wall around a garden | A loud alarm
exercise: «A blessing in disguise» means what? | A church service on Sunday | A gift wrapped in pretty paper | A plain, ordinary thing | * A bad thing that may turn out to be good
exercise: «Some April jokes are adverts in disguise.» What does in disguise mean here? | Very loud | Painted bright red | * Hidden, looking like something else | Given away free
test: «Toad was disguised as a washerwoman.» What does disguised mean? | Ran very fast down the road | Fell asleep in a chair | * Changed how he looked so no one knew him | Sang a song loudly
test: In a maths puzzle, what is a disguised number? | A number that is always zero | * A hidden number inside a sum or sentence that you must find | A number written in big letters | A number too big to count
exam: Mia says «Would you mind closing the window?» looks like a question, but it is a polite request. What is the sentence in disguise? | A rude command shouted across the room | A sum in disguise | * A polite request | A joke about the weather
